SHBUI changes by dishanhai, November 2026:
* Player-facing branding is SHBUI. The MuoniumPlayer Team and third-party contributors
  retain their respective copyrights.
  The original package names, protocol identifiers, configuration paths and preset formats
  are retained. Optional SHBUI theme and widget choices are local UI preferences.
* Player and room implementation compiled from source into the host. Loader events, mixins,
  resource discovery, native libraries and launch routes are integrated with SHBUI.
* Native widgets and fonts live in the UUK platform source root; theme, input and font
  callbacks are supplied by the host. Text fonts use SHBUI's licensed fonts; remapped
  Lucide glyphs retain their own notice in META-INF/third-party/lucide.
* The desktop directory picker uses LWJGL. Startup no longer installs separate mods,
  the optional Closure compiler or the Qishui companion. Original settings and media
  catalog identifiers are retained. Local YRC and ViPER kernels can be supplied by users.
* WAV random-access reads respect the data chunk's last complete sample. The embedded
  room engine preserves the mpsync wire format. Its license and notice are included.
  Direct invitations include the current room code and accept both the documented
  address:port#password#code form and the older four-segment form.
* Apple's full subscription playback remains with SHBUI's browser MusicKit integration.
  The embedded player's PCM route supports public previews and its provider fallback.
* Bundled MP devices/keys, third-party song lyrics, Apple font binaries, and
  personal-use impulse responses are excluded.
* Stock headphone surround uses the symmetric MIT KEMAR measurements by Bill
  Gardner and Keith Martin. The two SHBUI room presets use the University of
  Surrey's measured BRIRs. See META-INF/third-party/mit-kemar and surrey-brir
  for data-specific credits and terms. User-provided original kernels take precedence.
  The ViPER DSP implementation remains derived from NEURAX-FX/ViPERDSP and
  its upstream contributors, as noted in the individual source files.

